# The Lady's island, in the middle of the Silver Ford.

place the island
  title: The Lady's Island
  the sky: night
  the mist: light
  the ground: pebbles, 44 by 44 m
  you come in at 0 6, facing 0

  a river at 0 -15
  a river at 0 15
  a river at -15 0, turned 90
  a river at 15 0, turned 90
  a ferry boat at 3 10, turned 90
  Old Bram at 1 7.6, facing 200
  a shrine at 0 -4
  The Lady of the Ford at -1.8 -2.6, facing 30
  16 reeds between -9 -9 and 9 9
  6 rocks between -8 -8 and 8 8

  when you first arrive
    say: The boat bumps against the island. Bram holds it steady with the oar.
    Old Bram: I'll wait here. Don't keep her waiting, though. They say she's patient, but rivers aren't.

  when you talk to Old Bram
    Old Bram: Back across?
    choose
      choice: Yes, take me back.
        go to the ford
      choice: Not yet.
        Old Bram: I'm not going anywhere.

  when you talk to the Lady of the Ford
    if the lady gave her ember
      The Lady of the Ford: The river runs on. Go, little flame.
    otherwise
      The Lady of the Ford: A visitor. How long it has been since anyone rowed out with a gift.
      The Lady of the Ford: The river does not give. It only trades. What will you leave in the water for my ember?
      choose
        choice if you have the honey bread: Honey bread. It was a gift to me, so I'll give it to you.
          you lose the honey bread
          add 1 to kindness
          The Lady of the Ford: A gift passed on is worth twice a gift kept. Accepted.
          say: She dips her hand into the river and lifts out a coal that burns blue at its edges. With it comes a tiny silver bell, tangled in weed.
          you get the river ember
          you get the silver bell
          add 1 to embers
          put out the shrine
          remember the lady gave her ember
          The Lady of the Ford: The bell is for the Watcher on the peak. It only wakes for things that ring true. Bram knows the way upriver.
        choice: My fear. I've been scared all night. You can have it.
          add 1 to courage
          The Lady of the Ford: Fear is heavy. The river will carry it to the sea. Accepted.
          say: She dips her hand into the river and lifts out a coal that burns blue at its edges. With it comes a tiny silver bell, tangled in weed.
          you get the river ember
          you get the silver bell
          add 1 to embers
          put out the shrine
          remember the lady gave her ember
          The Lady of the Ford: The bell is for the Watcher on the peak. It only wakes for things that ring true. Bram knows the way upriver.
        choice: Nothing. I have nothing to spare.
          The Lady of the Ford: Then the river has nothing for you. Think again, lamp-carrier.

  when you look at the shrine
    if the lady gave her ember
      say: The shrine is dark now, but the stones are still warm.
    otherwise
      say: An old stone shrine. On top, a blue light turns slowly, like something under water.
